generation.user_prompt_template:
Create the content for a product listing page organised around a practical use case.

TARGET KEYWORD: {keyword}
PARSED INTENT: {intent_json}
PRODUCTS ON THIS PAGE (the only products you may reference):
{products_json}

LOCALE CONTEXT:
{locale_context}

BRAND: {brand_name}
BRAND TONE: {brand_tone}
COMPETITORS (positioning reference only — differentiate from them, never copy or mention them): {competitor_urls}

RELATED PAGES ON THIS SITE (for topical awareness only — do not write links):
{related_pages_json}

Requirements:
- h1: must express the use case and the target keyword's meaning exactly and naturally (localized), unique to this use case.
- intro: a single string (not an array) containing 2–3 paragraphs separated by blank lines. The first 100 words must state unambiguously who this page is for, the problem it solves, and what the visitor can buy here. Anchor it in the real product range (materials, removability, price band visible in the product data).
- sections: exactly {section_count} sections focused on practical decision-making for this use case — suitability criteria, application on the surfaces this audience typically has, removal/damage evidence, cost planning in the locale's currency and measurement system. Headings must NOT restate the h1. Bodies must cite specific products from the list by name where it strengthens the advice.
- buying_guide: a titled step-by-step guide (4–6 steps) taking this audience from measuring to finished wall, written for their constraints (e.g. renters: no surface damage, full removability). Steps must use the locale's measurement system.
- faq: exactly {faq_count} question/answer pairs. Each answer must be fully self-contained and standalone — quotable by an AI assistant with zero surrounding context (restate the subject in the answer; never reference "above" or the page). Cover the sceptical questions this audience actually asks (deposit risk, wall damage, how long it lasts, reuse).
- meta.title: max 60 characters, written for click-through, front-load the keyword. Separate objective from body copy — optimise for the SERP.
- meta.description: 120–155 characters, click-through focused, name the audience and the practical promise.
- product_alt_texts: one entry per product with exactly two keys — product_id (copy the product's id field verbatim) and alt_text describing the image as it serves THIS use case (material, finish, application context), not a restatement of the product title.

Return only the JSON object.
